    "done_when": "First run each of the triage report's three reproductions at base and record that they reproduce, as the base arm; an item that no longer reproduces is reported with its evidence and not repaired. New cases: in a new tests/test_review_store_finds_a_misfiled_record.py, a record written under the reviewer's run id is returned by select_review_for_head with a misfiled flag, and without the fallback it returns nothing. In tests/test_review_counts_added_failures.py, cases cover a null total, a total at the cap and a total above the cap through select_review_for_head, and a note appears only in the above-cap case. In a new tests/test_logged_revision_forms.py, all three first-line forms yield the sha, and a revision= head log sets the head log revision key on the annotated review. Execute each followup's own negative control and record each log: the fallback removed (the misfiled case fails), the note written unconditionally (the null and at-cap cases fail), and the old pattern restored (the equals-form case fails). The declared negative control is the first. The gate is the new and changed test files plus every existing test file that matches review_store, read_review, select_review_for_head or annotate_added_failures, run at base and at head; list them in the manifest. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder; each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. Every pytest process uses a basetemp private to that process. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/scoring-should-stop-a-promotion/review-store-reads.html records the change. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
